{
  "dom_id": "step-q142945",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
  "worked_solution": "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)=\\frac{P(X=x,Y=4)}{P(Y=4)}=\\frac{f(x,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $x\\in {1,2,3},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(2,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.05}{0.2}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=3\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(3,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.05}{0.2}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
